<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105753" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρῠφ-ή</span></b> , ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θρύπτω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>softness, delicacy, daintiness,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				892.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				900e
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στολίδος κροκόεσσαν . .
				τρυφάν</span> (sic leg. pro <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στολίδα .
				. τρυφᾶς</span>) <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				1491
			</span></i> (lyr.): pl., <i>luxuries, daintinesses,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. Τρωϊκαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Or.</u>
					1113
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρυφὰς τοιάσδε [τρυφᾶν</span>]
				<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ba.</u>
				970
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ ἄγαν τ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					54.2
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς πλούτους ἀποβλέψαι καὶ τ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Alc.</u>
					1.122c
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Lg.</u>
				637e
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>luxuriousness, wantonness,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν γυναικῶν ἡ τ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Lys.</u>
					387
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. καὶ ἀκολασία, τ. καὶ μαλθακία,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Grg.</u>
				492c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>R.</u>
				590b
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ἐν ἡμέρᾳ τ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>2 Ep.Pet.</u>
					2.13
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπερτεταμένη τ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sor.
					2.54
				</span></i>
			: personified, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τρυφῆς πρόσωπον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ec.</u>
					973
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Alex.
				230.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>daintiness, fastidiousness,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ τρυφῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Pl.</u>
					818
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕβρις ταῦτ᾽ ἐστὶ καὶ πολλὴ τ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ra.</u>
					21
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Grg.</u>
				525a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1295b17
			</span></i>.</div>
